# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS. Nothing here may ever reach the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
lta_key.txt
*key*.txt
*.key
.env
.env.*
secrets*
credentials*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
logs/
data/temp/

# Excel lock files. Left behind when Excel crashes, and they break the writer.
~$*.xlsx
.*.writing.xlsx

# Working copies the scripts set aside when a file is unreadable or its header
# changed. Useful locally, not worth committing.
*.corrupt-*
*.schema-*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILT WORKBOOKS. Not committed, on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An .xlsx is a zip: git cannot diff it, so every change stores a whole new
# copy. They are also derived - run_local.py rebuilds any of them from the
# CSVs in seconds - and git should hold sources, not build output.
#
# The real reason it matters here: GitHub's daily run and your local run both
# write output/utilisation/utilisation_log.xlsx. If that file were tracked,
# every git pull after a local build would collide on a binary that cannot be
# merged. Ignoring it removes the collision entirely.
#
# You can still get workbooks without building them: Actions publishes them as
# artifacts on every run. See GITHUB_SETUP.md section 6.
output/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What IS committed, for the record:
#   data/raw/ev, data/raw/carpark    gzipped snapshots, the audit trail
#   data/utilisation/               the hourly series, fact and dim
#   *.py, *.yml, *.md               the code and the docs
# Workbooks are NOT committed - see the block above.
# If the repository gets uncomfortably large, the first thing to drop is
# data/raw. Uncomment the next line to stop committing it.
# data/raw/
